On the weapons front, tourists can become Expert at dagger,
Skilled at silver saber and #twoweponing, plus Basic at
nearly every imaginable weapon class.  For fun they can
get to Skilled at unicorn horn.  At a distraction they can
get Expert at dart.

So select dagger, saber and twoweapon.  Advance each to
Basic before advancing other stuff.  Advance each to
Skilled before advancing other stuff.  Advance dagger to
expert when you have the skill slots to spare in order to
become a walking machine gun with a stack of elven daggers.
Gather plenty of eleven daggers to have a full quiver.
Early on there will be plenty of orcish and regular ones,
so use them for the advancement but save the enchantment
for the eleven ones (and Magicbane if you get that gift).

Those skills in addition to advancing to basic in whatever
artifact weapon you receive as a gift.  Tourists by default
are Neutral but you never know for an individual tourist.
Neutrals don't get Werebane or Greyswandir.  Nonetheless,
do your best to get a silver saber from an (un)cooperative
watch captain or captain because later in the game silver
saber makes a fabulous secondary weapon and Tourist can
twoweapon.

On the armor front, since tourists can twoweapon don't put
too much consideration into a shield.  That means your 2
options for reflection are amulet or SDSM.  That choice
influences how you will get MR (and if you get Magicbane
get it redundant).  [oMR looks good for a tourist.

The tourist Quest artifact does charging.  This makes
rings and wands much more powerfull in the late game.
Gather interesting rings (not that that's different
advice from other classes).

